    "explanation": "To both parties: the cancellation fee of SGD 4.50 is refunded in full to the rider, and no driver compensation is payable.\n\nThe deciding fact is the cancellation reason code. The trip record (EV-TRIP-02747) shows the driver terminated the trip at 11:28:47 under reason code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE. POL-NS-01 limb (d) requires termination under RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT, and the clause says in terms that DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE is the driver's own admission that he could not find the rider and does not satisfy limb (d). The fee therefore fails at the fourth limb and is not chargeable. The driver's counterparty statement ('Could not locate the rider so I cancelled') is the same concession.\n\nBecause the driver's stationary fixes lie INSIDE the STANDARD arrival radius of 50 m — the GPS trace (EV-GPS-02747) shows one continuous in-geofence run of 380 seconds, 11:22:26 to 11:28:46, with 39 qualifying fixes and no gaps — POL-NS-01 fixes the outcome on its own: the fee is not chargeable, the ruling is FULL_REFUND of the cancellation fee with no driver compensation, and the mis-selected reason code is recorded for driver education. That is the referral above.\n\nFor the driver's side, I accept these points but none of them saves the fee: the dwell of 380 seconds did exceed the 180-second free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180); the arrival marker at 11:22:26 coincides to the second with the first qualifying in-geofence fix, so there is no clock skew and POL-NS-05's false-arrival test is not engaged; the stationary fixes were inside the radius, not at a wrong entrance, so POL-NS-03 does not apply; the GPS artifact is COMPLETE with weight 1.0 and no impairment; and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d = 2, below 4; rate 2/138 = 0.014, below 0.08). But POL-NS-07 compensation only follows where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and it is not.\n\nFor the rider's side, I accept the decisive limb (d) failure, and independently the POL-NS-04 route: the rider was present and coordinating — her track (EV-GPS-02747) places her device within roughly 13 to 19 m of the pin across 65 qualifying fixes, inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius, and she sent 'at the lift lobby' at 11:23:26 in reply to the driver's 'cannot find you, where are you' at 11:22:56 — and the driver neither replied within 120 seconds nor made an in-app call before cancelling at 11:28:47. The POL-NS-06 shortfall route does not apply, as the rider herself accepts, because the dwell exceeded the minimum.\n\nTwo claims about the missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-02747-01, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) were discarded at the mechanical stage for citing an impaired artifact without naming its issue code; nothing in this ruling turns on the advisory, which neither side relies on.\n\nThe figure refunded is the cancellation-fee line of SGD 4.50 on EV-FARE-02747 (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). The monetary effect of SGD 4.50 is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00 and executes automatically. Confidence is 0.9, capped at 1.0 because every artifact carrying the deciding facts — EV-TRIP-02747, EV-GPS-02747, EV-CHAT-02747 and EV-FARE-02747 — has weight_multiplier 1.0. The escalation triggers of POL-NS-09 do not fire: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, no no-show disputes between these parties in 90 days, and no abuse pattern on either profile."
